- AC16 (R4): In a run with `audio` verified, the request following an
  `audio.capture` observation carries exactly one audio input part (format
  `wav`, decoded bytes equal to the stored attachment) plus the transcription
  text when present, and no trace or event emitted during the run contains
  the base64 payload or a filesystem path; in a run without `audio`
  verified, an `audio_ref` with a transcription produces a request carrying
  the transcription text and 0 audio parts, with `brain.run.completed`
  carrying `audio_omitted: 1`; an `audio_ref` without transcription ends the
  run `error` with `failure: capability_missing`, `capability: audio`, 0
